## Block

- No production file changed. No implementation commit exists.
- This Green run stopped on the Rule "a committed Red test must not be edited; stop and return
  blocked when a Red test contradicts the specification".
- The block is in `apps/storytime/__tests__/phase3-decodable-ui.test.tsx` at lines 90 to 93:

```ts
const clips = played.filter((src) => src.includes("phonemes/daniel/"));
expect(clips).toHaveLength(blendPlanForWord(word!, cvc).graphemes.length);
expect(clips.map((src) => src.split("/").at(-1)?.replace(/^\d{2}-/, "").replace(/\.mp3$/, "")))
  .toEqual(blendPlanForWord(word!, cvc).graphemes);
```

- The contract conflict: `blendPlanForWord` must give letter graphemes (`["p", "a", "n"]` for `pan`),
  because the Phase 2 test asserts `plan.graphemes.join("") === word.toLowerCase()`. The phoneme
  bank must hold the G3 names, so the `/a/` clip is `phonemes/daniel/26-a-short.mp3`. The test strips
  only `NN-` and `.mp3`, so the clip name becomes `a-short`, and it cannot equal the grapheme `a`.
- The first shipped blend word is `pan` in `w03` (`Nan` in `w02` also blends after the F28 case).
  Both words hold the grapheme `a`. No real bank clip for `a` is named `NN-a.mp3`; only
  `26-a-short.mp3` exists. The test passes only if the UI plays a media path that has no file.
- One-line fix at line 92: compare against the bank file, or allow the G3 variant suffix:

```ts
expect(clips.map((src) => src.split("/").at(-1)?.replace(/^\d{2}-/, "").replace(/(-[a-z]+)?\.mp3$/, "")))
```

- With that fix the Green work is small. The planned implementation is ready: the `StorytimeDecodable`
  client component, the 45-clip `PHONEME_BANK`, the `blendPlanForWord` F28 fix (loop maximum and
  lower-case segmentation for a capital word), and the route wiring.

